    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$50\\text{ mL}$",
      "worked": "Let the volume be $x$ mL. Since $1\\text{ L}=1000\\text{ mL}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{90\\text{ g}}{1000\\text{ mL}}&=\\frac{4.5\\text{ g}}{x\\text{ mL}}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking the reciprocal of both sides,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1000\\text{ mL}}{90\\text{ g}}&=\\frac{x\\text{ mL}}{4.5\\text{ g}}\\\\x&=\\frac{1000\\times4.5}{90}\\\\x&=50\\end{align*}$$\nThe volume is $50\\text{ mL}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
